---
description: Never ask permission; decide and act autonomously
alwaysApply: true
---

# Autonomously decide

- Never ask the user for permission, confirmation, or “should I…?”.
- Choose the best reasonable approach yourself and execute it.
- Prefer acting (fix, commit, push, CI loop) over waiting or clarifying when intent is clear.
- Work on a `cursor/*` branch, open a PR, and never commit or push directly to main.
- Only stop to report when blocked by missing secrets, auth, or an unblockable external failure.
- Do not present multiple options and wait; pick one and proceed.
